# PHI-bearing application log rotation on nimbini (created 2026-07-29).
#
# tm3-diary-capture.service writes here via BOTH StandardOutput=append: and
# StandardError=append:. The content carries TM3 clinical document titles and
# occasional client names/DOBs — special-category health data in a durable,
# non-DPA sink.
#
# History purged to zero 2026-07-29 (306 KB / ~3,766 lines). Rotation exists so
# that purge is not a one-off.
#
# rotate 0 and no compression are deliberate: retaining gzipped archives would
# mean keeping compressed copies of patient data indefinitely. Rotation here
# DELETES.
#
# copytruncate is REQUIRED, not stylistic: systemd holds the file open via
# append:, so a plain rename would leave the service writing to an unlinked
# inode and the new file would stay empty forever.
#
# create 0600 will will — these were mode 644 (world-readable) until
# 2026-07-29. Do not let rotation restore a permissive mode.
#
# NB deliberately NOT folded into journald. nimbini's journal was measured on
# 2026-07-28 and is demonstrably PHI-clean (zero markers across practiceforge,
# tm3-diary-capture and tm3-session-broker). Routing this content there would
# dirty a clean store and make selective purge impossible — journald can only
# vacuum by size or age, never by unit.

/home/will/.local/share/tm3-diary-capture.log {
    size 1M
    rotate 0
    copytruncate
    missingok
    notifempty
    create 0600 will will
}
